data.content:
Your `ReportGenerator` has **four** categories of static dependencies: **File system** (`File.WriteAllText`, `Directory.Exists`, `Directory.CreateDirectory`), **Time** (`DateTime.UtcNow`), **Environment** (`Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable`, `Environment.MachineName`), and **Console** (`Console.WriteLine`).

Here's the recommended approach for each:

---

### 1. File System → `System.IO.Abstractions` (NuGet)

Install the package:
```
dotnet add package System.IO.Abstractions
```

Inject `IFileSystem` and use `fileSystem.File.*` / `fileSystem.Directory.*`:
```csharp
public class ReportGenerator(IFileSystem fileSystem)
{
    // fileSystem.File.WriteAllText(path, content);
    // fileSystem.Directory.Exists(dir);
    // fileSystem.Directory.CreateDirectory(dir);
    // fileSystem.Path.Combine(a, b);
}
```

For tests, install the testing helpers:
```
dotnet add <TestProject> package System.IO.Abstractions.TestingHelpers
```
```csharp
var mockFs = new MockFileSystem();
var generator = new ReportGenerator(mockFs);
```

---

### 2. Time → `TimeProvider` (built-in on .NET 10)

No extra package needed. Register in DI:
```csharp
builder.Services.AddSingleton(TimeProvider.System);
```

Inject and replace `DateTime.UtcNow` with:
```csharp
timeProvider.GetUtcNow()
```

For tests, use `FakeTimeProvider` from:
```
dotnet add <TestProject> package Microsoft.Extensions.TimeProvider.Testing
```

---

### 3. Environment → Custom `IEnvironmentProvider`

No built-in abstraction exists. Generate a minimal wrapper covering only the two members you use:

**Interface** — place in `Services/`:
```csharp
namespace NeedsWrappers.Services;

public interface IEnvironmentProvider
{
    string? GetEnvironmentVariable(string variable);
    string MachineName { get; }
}
```

**Implementation:**
```csharp
namespace NeedsWrappers.Services;

public sealed class EnvironmentProvider : IEnvironmentProvider
{
    public string? GetEnvironmentVariable(string variable)
        => Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable(variable);

    public string MachineName => Environment.MachineName;
}
```

**DI registration:**
```csharp
builder.Services.AddSingleton<IEnvironmentProvider, EnvironmentProvider>();
```

---

### 4. Console → Custom `IConsole`

Same pattern — wrap only `WriteLine`:

```csharp
public interface IConsole
{
    void WriteLine(string message);
}

public sealed class SystemConsole : IConsole
{
    public void WriteLine(string message)
        => Console.WriteLine(message);
}
```

```csharp
builder.Services.AddSingleton<IConsole, SystemConsole>();
```

---

### Refactored `ReportGenerator`

After all four are injectable:

```csharp
public class ReportGenerator(
    IFileSystem fileSystem,
    TimeProvider timeProvider,
    IEnvironmentProvider environment,
    IConsole console)
{
    public string GenerateReport(string reportName)
    {
        var timestamp = timeProvider.GetUtcNow().ToString("yyyyMMdd_HHmmss");
        var outputDir = environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("REPORT_OUTPUT_DIR") ?? "/tmp/reports";

        if (!fileSystem.Directory.Exists(outputDir))
            fileSystem.Directory.CreateDirectory(outputDir);

        var reportPath = fileSystem.Path.Combine(outputDir, $"{reportName}_{timestamp}.txt");
        var content = $"Report: {reportName}\nGenerated: {timeProvider.GetUtcNow():O}\nMachine: {environment.MachineName}";

        fileSystem.File.WriteAllText(reportPath, content);
        console.WriteLine($"Report written to {reportPath}");

        return reportPath;
    }
}
```

